  "_comment": "Manual per-ticker overrides applied on top of the live provider. `price` is a FALLBACK only (live wins). IV is now DERIVED per-stock from a `dcf` assumption block (services/dcf.ts): each name gets its own eps0 (anchor forward EPS/FCF-per-share), near-term growth, terminalGrowth, discountRate, and optional netCashPerShare — so a wide-moat compounder, a margin-inflecting platform, and a cyclical commodity are valued differently, and every assumption is visible/editable. base/bear/best are computed (bear = +1% discount & 0.7x growth; best = -1% discount & 1.3x growth). Assumptions set 2026-06-27, aligned to per-stock theses (NVDA Blackwell/Rubin, SE profitability inflection, TCEHY steady + China premium, MU normalized mid-cycle EPS). Change any number and the IV recomputes on restart. A plain `iv:{base,bear,best}` still works if no `dcf` block. Canadian (.TO) names carry sourced price/PE/forwardPE/peg; other US names are price-only.",
